Hmm...  I just typed out a response on google, but there was a server
error when I tried to post.  The rng is extending its sphere
influence.

Anyway, key points from that response:

Ghennom is a Sisyphean task, and therefore frustrating.

Your ideas for altering level layout and/or reducing number of levels
sound good.

However, the real problem is that the player has nothing to gain by
doing Gehennom - the only aim is to get to the bottom, get the amulet,
and get out.

Drawing on another YANI I read recently, I suggest having an item
generated somewhere in Gehennom that gives the passwall ability.  It
must only be available in Gehennom - not available by wishing or
anything else.  It can be activated every [100-200] turns and will
provide passwall for a limited number of turns once activated. 
Without this limitation the Plane of Earth becomes trivial and the
Astral Plane becomes an awful lot easier.

Why is this item necessary?  I suggest the deepest altar (the one
guarded by the high priest of Moloch who has the amulet) should be
surrounded by undiggable walls.  Instead of having to find the secret
door to get in, the player should have to have the passwall ability. 
The reason I haven't suggested that the item has a limited number of
charges is because that would make it possible to get "stuck" in the
little room with the altar.

Of course, this item isn't absolutely necessary - for example
polymorphing into a Xorn will get you in as well.  However, one of the
best things about nethack is being able to do things in a number of
different ways.

